- Then P-5 (§10), P-4 (§9), P-6 (§11/§14/§18) in order, each with golden + negative controls, isolated-DB migrations, and evidence files.

### 4. Five research candidates (SPEC §7)
funding_open_interest_squeeze, liquidity_sweep_reversal, volatility_compression_breakout, btc_eth_lead_lag, multi_timeframe_trend_following — research cohorts only, NOT new primary accounts. Reuse Go engine; enforce §7.7 mechanical look-ahead controls (HTF closure, causal mutation test, negative future-feature control) and §7.8 valid negative outcomes.

### 5. A0–A3 autonomy (SPEC §8)
A0 registry → A1 versioned paper challenger controller → A2 Gate-6-gated local paper promotion (feature flag OFF; expect NOT_ELIGIBLE/SHADOW_HISTORY_ABSENT) → A3 research-only allocation. No real orders; P-3 rejected-signal replay remains PROHIBITED.

### 6. Final regression + evidence
Full PHPUnit, Pint, Vue tests/build, Go unit/race/vet; endpoint smoke on test env; RFC §9.3 evidence schemas; §11 final report format.

## Hard prohibitions (unchanged)
No live orders/trade keys; no production deploy/migrations/CI/SSH; no git push/commit/reset/clean; no ECONOM access; no docker/sudo; no P-3 replay; do not alter the eight primary ledgers; never fabricate metrics.

## Suggested launch
`MAX_HOURS=10` with future SOFT/HARD deadlines so implementation actually begins before shutdown. Start at Step 3 (P-2 finish) since WIP already exists, then Step 1 audits, then 2, then 4, then 5.
