- P-6 gate rules: fail-closed, fixed gate order, `NULL` never means “good”; P-1 is attribution-only (no ESS requirement); P-4/P-5 must declare their own sample/coverage; P-3 input and risk-rejected-opportunity claims are refused (`P3_NOT_AUTHORIZED`); `REJECTED`/`EVIDENCE_NEGATIVE` require an explicit registered test outcome; `OWNER_APPROVED_FOR_SEPARATE_PAPER_EXPERIMENT` requires a previous `ELIGIBLE_FOR_OWNER_REVIEW` plus actor+authorization hash; decision records are append-only.
- A0–A3 decision: overnight spec §8 authorizes sequential gated engineering (A0 → A1 → A2 local flag-off → A3 research-only); master spec §4.8 labels A0–A3 “NOT APPROVED” but the overnight spec is this session’s contract. A2 must fail closed to `NOT_ELIGIBLE / SHADOW_HISTORY_ABSENT`; feature flags OFF by default; A3 must never increase total risk, merge ledgers or write a budget.
- Offline evidence scripts embed `generated_at_utc`, so regenerating changes the SHA-256 — always re-hash and update the report after the final run.
- SQLite decimal columns return unnormalized strings; compare DB decimals via `BigDecimal::of(...)->isEqualTo(...)`, not string equality.

